{"questions":[{"question_id":"yLM7mSC8LrFHWos6","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2013 (Offline)","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"mathematics","chapter":"statistics","chapterGroup":"algebra","topic":"calculation-of-standard-deviation-variance-and-mean-deviation-of-grouped-and-ungrouped-data","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"all-the-students-of-a-class-performed-poorly-in-mathematics-2013-marks-4-ylm7msc8lrfhwos6.htm","content":"All the students of a class performed poorly in Mathematics. The teacher decided to give grace marks of 10\nto each of the students. Which of the following statistical measures will not change even after the grace\nmarks were given? ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"median"},{"identifier":"B","content":"mode"},{"identifier":"C","content":"variance"},{"identifier":"D","content":"mean "}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"As we know variance does not change with the change of origin. So, here even after adding grace marks <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.557ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 1000 688\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, the variance will be same. \n<br><br>Let's see with an example, \n<br><br>Assume initial variance <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.881ex\" height=\"3.481ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1193.5 4809.4 1538.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"curr